    "label": "OVERHANG VARIANT (not App output)",
    "note": "Vector 2. One occurrence whose source-window child is longer than the occurrence, so clampToOccurrenceDuration is exercised. It reuses the native shot-1 revision (clip-a: at 1, hold 4, from 2, to 6, speed 2, so 2 s on the timeline). occ-c starts at 2 s and lasts 1.5 s, so its window is [2, 3.5) s. The child is absolute [3, 5) s, which overhangs the occurrence end by 1.5 s. The parent and its ordinary clips are the native payload unchanged.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "occurrence_id": "occ-c",
        "shot_id": "chapter-shot",
        "shot_revision_id": "shot-1",
        "placement": {
          "start_ms": 2000,
          "track": "picture"
        },
        "duration_ms": 1500,
        "source_offset": 0,
        "speed": 1,
        "track": "picture"
      }
    ],
    "clamp": {
      "on": "The compiler's only policy (03:46 decision): visible end = min(child end, occurrence end) = 3.5 s.",
      "off": "The unclamped child end, 5 s. The compiler has no clamp-off mode; this row is the App per-call option's output, computed from the authored child and not emitted by the compiler."
    },
